# Gandhigram Rural Institute (GRI) Mobile Portal — Supabase Cloud Configuration
#
# HOW BACKEND CONFIGURATION WORKS
# The Flutter app reads backend credentials at compile time via --dart-define
# (NOT from a .env file at runtime). Copy your credentials from:
#   https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/<your-project-ref>/settings/api
#
# Run / build with credentials (PowerShell):
#   flutter run `
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co `
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-public-key>
#
# Or Bash/macOS/Linux:
#   flutter run \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co \
#     --dart-define=SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-anon-public-key>
#
# Without these flags the app runs in fully-functional OFFLINE-VAULT mode:
# all institutional data persists on-device (see services/local_data_store_service.dart)
# and cloud features simply degrade gracefully.
#
# SECURITY NOTES
# - Use the anon/public key only. NEVER expose the service_role key in a client app.
# - Row Level Security is enforced by supabase/migrations/*.sql for every table.
# - Verify schema after connecting:
#     supabase link --project-ref <ref>
#     supabase db push
